{"nodes": [{"id": "title", "type": "text", "text": "Module 19 — Threat Assessment with Attack Surface Analysis\ndefinition → visualize → IoEs → simulate → reduce → cloud + IoT", "x": -1200, "y": -3600, "width": 2400, "height": 70, "color": "5"}, {"id": "b1", "type": "text", "text": "LO01 · CONCEPT  (pp4-9)\n\nSURFACE = SUM of all possible\nexposures (KNOWN, UNKNOWN, POTENTIAL)\n  protocols · interfaces · input fields ·\n  services · unpatched · open ports ·\n  misconfig · excess privilege · bad\n  segmentation · unaware employees\n  smaller = safer; keep MINIMUM\n\n5 CATEGORIES\n  Network (unauthenticated interfaces)\n  Software (code/config)\n  Physical (direct hardware)\n  Human (WEAKEST POINT)\n  System (OS entries; more = bigger)\n\nUNENCRYPTED: Telnet FTP HTTP SMTP\n  (+ NFS SMB netdump, printers)\n  unpatched Java/Adobe; USB laptops;\ndiscarded drives\n\nANALYSIS = assessment of exploitable\nvulns; 4 STEPS: Visualize → IoEs →\nSimulate → Reduce", "x": -2400, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b2", "type": "text", "text": "LO02 · VISUALIZE  (pp10-17)\n\nidentify ASSETS, TOPOLOGIES, POLICIES\n  mapped elements: servers, data flows,\n  vulnerable-asset paths\n  challenges: no correlation tooling,\n  policy opacity, SECURITY SILOS\n\nTHREATPATH (pp14-15)\n  lateral-movement topo map; 4 defender\nactions; early-exposure benefits\n  attivonetworks.com (prose form)\nSKYBOX (pp16-17)\n  true visibility; 3 key features\n  captures pp13-16 = NON-EVIDENCE", "x": -1740, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b3", "type": "text", "text": "LO03 · IoE SYSTEM + APP  (pp18-25)\n\nIoE = POTENTIAL RISK EXPOSURES\nattackers breach with\n  ID incl. firewall-rule events\n\nSYSTEM (pp21-24)\n  ATTACK SURFACE ANALYZER\n  (9 components, GUI/CLI/SQLite)\n  WINDOWS SANDBOX TOOL\n  (14-tool table: DumpProcessMitigations,\n  NewProcessFromToken, Win8+)\n\nAPPLICATION (pp25-27)\n  OWASP ASD: endpoints, STATIC ROUTE\n  PARSING (p26, sibling), version diffs,\n  ZAP/Burp/CLI, BApp Store\n  owasp.org (body form)\n  THREATMODELER (channels/widgets/engine)", "x": -1080, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b4", "type": "text", "text": "LO03 · IoE NETWORK + HUMAN  (pp26-33)\n\nNETWORK (pp28-30)\n  ATTACKSURFACEMAPPER\n  (OSINT + active; URL unprintable)\n  AMASS (techniques/sources; Table 19.1\n  w/o column claims; Fig 19.7 refused)\n\nHUMAN (pp31-33)\n  OhPhish · SPF · SoSafe · SET ·\n  PhishGrid · Frenzy · GoPhish\n  bare-but-printed github Sources;\n  'hosing' kept verbatim\n  app tail (pp26-27) placed as-sourced", "x": -420, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700, "color": "3"}, {"id": "b5", "type": "text", "text": "LO04 · SIMULATE  (pp34-41)\n\nvalidate + manage CONTROLS; assess\nflaws BEFORE attacks; how IoEs become\nEXPLOITS; attacker-view check\n  single unit viewed, ONE target hit\n  recon → servers/services; SE +\n  phishing sim + exfil testing\n  SMALL CHANGE answers 5 questions\n  (paths, moves, topo, policy, direction)\n\nBAS TOOLS (prose only)\n  INFECTION MONKEY (random-server)\n  CYMULATE (one-click + APT)\n  PHISHTHREAT (9 languages)\n  PICUS (detection testing, SIEM tune)\n  SAFEBREACH (continuous validation)\n  FIREMON (change/compliance)\n  WHITEHAX (readiness verification)\n  ✗ AttackIQ/CyCognito/XM = tile-only", "x": 240, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b6", "type": "text", "text": "LO05 · REDUCE  (pp42-48)\n\nASR = CLOSE ALL BUT NEEDED DOORS\n  fewer vulns = less compromise\n  app: kill redundant functions, ENTRY\n  POINTS, APIs, code, complexity\n  SIMPLEST CODE, LEAST ASSUMPTIONS\n  BROWSER disable-list (p45): traversal,\n  prediction, cloud sharing, sync,\n  popups, 3D, JS, autocomplete, cookies,\n  metrics, incognito, cleartext pw,\n  pw manager, plugins, 3rd-party cookies\n  + revocation checks, safe browsing,\n  whitelists, encryption\n  PORTS: audit with NMAP first (Unicorn,\n  Angry IP, Netcat); close public extras\n  HUMAN: periodic training → CIA;\n  6-question program", "x": -2400, "y": -2620, "width": 620, "height": 700, "color": "4"}, {"id": "b7", "type": "text", "text": "LO06 · CLOUD  (pp49-53)\n\nmore cloud + IoT = MORE ENDPOINTS\n  3 PARTICIPANTS: users · instances /\n  services · provider (≥2 interact)\n\n6 SURFACES\n  Service→User (client-server: overflow,\n  SQLi) · User→Service (browser/cache/\n  phishing) · Cloud→Service (exhaustion)\n  Service→Cloud (provider-on-instance =\n  MOST CRITICAL) · Cloud→User (control\n  plane) · User→Cloud (FAKE USAGE BILL)\n\n7 RECOMMENDATIONS (p52)\n  map ALL assets + both infras · know\n  every vuln/misconfig · local+cloud\n  controls · EVERY endpoint · ALL repos ·\n  contract BEFORE THE SLA", "x": -1740, "y": -2620, "width": 620, "height": 700}, {"id": "b8", "type": "text", "text": "LO06 · IoT + SUMMARY  (pp54-59)\n\nsurface = IoT + app + device vulns\n  OWASP areas (owasp.org): access control\n  (implicit trust) · MEMORY (clear-text\n  creds) · PHYSICAL (firmware extraction,\n  console) · WEB (scope only) · FIRMWARE\n  (DEFAULT CREDS, botnets) · NETWORK\n  (inject/DoS/MitM) · ADMIN (SQLi/XSS/\n  enum/weak pw) · STORAGE (unencrypted)\n  · CLOUD-WEB (NO 2FA) · BACKEND APIs\n  (PII leaks) · UPDATES (unsigned) ·\n  MOBILE (implicit trust) · VENDOR APIs ·\n  ECO-COMMS (cascade) · TRAFFIC\n\nIoT 7 (p58): Secure-by-Design buy ·\npre-connect review · secure config ·\nminimize · segment/IAM · physical ·\nmonitor\n\nSUMMARY (p59): exposures sum ·\nassets/topos/policies · ThreatPath +\nsecuriCAD + Skybox · patch + RETEST", "x": -1080, "y": -2620, "width": 620, "height": 700}, {"id": "pat", "type": "text", "text": "THE MODULE'S FIVE TRAPS\n\n1 · PIPELINE ORDER\n  Visualize → IoEs → Simulate →\n  Reduce — 'what next' = stage order\n2 · KNOWN + UNKNOWN + POTENTIAL\n  never 'known only'; analysis assesses,\n  REDUCTION implements\n3 · SPLIT SENTENCES\n  ASD capabilities span pp25-26; app tail\n  sits in pp26-27 — cite actual pages\n4 · TILE-ONLY NAMES\n  AttackIQ/CyCognito/XM Cyber, pp46-47\n  tables: omitted per scope, never options\n5 · UNPRINTABLE / VERBATIM\n  ASM URL omitted; 'hosing', bare github\n  URLs, IPv41nfo kept — 'which printed'\n  items use exact forms", "x": -420, "y": -2620, "width": 1320, "height": 700, "color": "6"}], "edges": [{"id": "e1", "fromNode": "b1", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b2", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e2", "fromNode": "b2", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b3", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e3", "fromNode": "b3", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b4", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e4", "fromNode": "b4", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b5", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e5", "fromNode": "b5", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "b6", "toSide": "top"}, {"id": "e6", "fromNode": "b6", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b7", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e7", "fromNode": "b7", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b8", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e8", "fromNode": "b8", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "pat", "toSide": "left"}]}